<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  ============================================================================
  ensemble-watchdog-watcher.plist — launchd AGENT (not daemon) for the
  watchdog-watcher (Auto-Restart Phase 1, plan §4.6 m3 / §6 row
  "Watchdog (supervisor) dies").

  This is a REPO TEMPLATE, not an installed file. It contains literal
  INSTALL_DIR_PLACEHOLDER tokens (same convention as
  scripts/ensemble-prod.plist). `make watchdog-install` stages it with
  the real path substituted and copies it to ~/Library/LaunchAgents —
  the printed launchctl bootstrap command activates it.

  Why an AGENT and not part of the daemon's launchd job: this watches
  for the case where the supervisor configuration itself is broken
  (unloaded/typo'd plist) — the very case where nothing inside the
  launchd job tree is alive to say anything. A separate
  StartInterval-driven agent survives that class of failure by
  construction (launchd runs it regardless of the daemon job's state).

  Division of labor:
    launchd job (ensemble-prod.plist) — supervises the launcher/daemon.
    THIS agent — every 300s, probes ONLY /livez (never /readyz —
    readiness never triggers action, ADR-003) and notifies via macOS
    Notification Center when the daemon has been absent >600s. It
    NEVER restarts or signals anything. Since P2.3 B4 (ADR-025(b)) the
    same agent also file-watches two daemon-DOWN channels — the
    launcher burst-abort marker (.launcher-state) and terminal journal
    events (releases/state.json halt/sweep_rollback) — best-effort,
    skipped silently where those files do not exist yet. See
    scripts/watchdog-watcher.sh for the full contract and the Phase-6
    (LLM observer, ADR-008) attach point.

  DEMO USAGE (3-env topology): duplicate with Label
  com.ensemble.watchdog.demo and the demo INSTALL_DIR — the port comes
  from each install's staged .env (nothing to edit here; ADR-014).

  INSTALL_DIR is REQUIRED and passed EXPLICITLY in ProgramArguments —
  watchdog-watcher.sh is explicit-only (no default anywhere, promotion
  ladder U6): a staged plist missing the install-dir argument fails the
  watcher's usage gate (nonzero exit, logged) instead of silently
  watching the live install. Duplicate this plist per env with the
  env's own dir; never rely on a fallback.

  Health endpoint: http://127.0.0.1:9797/livez (port resolved from
  INSTALL_DIR/.env at run time, canonical 9797 — D1 FINAL).
  ============================================================================
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.ensemble.watchdog</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>INSTALL_DIR_PLACEHOLDER/scripts/watchdog-watcher.sh</string>
        <string>INSTALL_DIR_PLACEHOLDER</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Every 5 minutes: absent-episodes are detected within 10–15 min
         (threshold 600s measured from the FIRST miss the watcher
         observed). Deliberately NOT RunAtLoad-quiet: an early check at
         load time also verifies the watcher itself was installed. -->
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>300</integer>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>INSTALL_DIR_PLACEHOLDER/data/watchdog.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>INSTALL_DIR_PLACEHOLDER/data/watchdog.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
